Z||000000||Smoooooth GT||09-09-2001||08:28 AM||||Hellllllooo....<BR>My mom keep's asking me(she loves to look at the forum)...  why, alot of people LOVE Fiero's soooo much, YET, we want to modify(side scoop's trunk scoop's, motor swap's,etc.) our car's???  If we love Fiero's so much, then why change them?????<BR>help me answer her...lol    Thank's for your input...    Steve<P>ps.  but, she loves the Smoooooth GT... yet, it's modified...lol<P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cozmo||09-09-2001||08:33 AM||||It's the last American streetrod.<BR>There hasn't been any other car made in the last 20 years that you can do sooo much COOL STUFF to... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BobC||||reg||14
Z||000002||Formula||09-09-2001||04:19 PM||||its a cheap sports car with a huge aftermarket...<P>'nough said...<P>btw... civics are cheap with a huge aftermarket but they arent sports cars.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||09-09-2001||04:49 PM||||Well, it's like this...there's so many of us here that like this car, yet we don't all want to be the same. So everyone likes to do something to be different, though we're all still alike. Did that make sense?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">        <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC (FOR SALE)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Urchin||09-09-2001||04:54 PM||||When it comes to engine mods and minor body mods that don't drastically effect the appearance of the car I can understand.  But to be honest, I have wondered the same thing... why people who love fieros put body kits on them ie. ferraris, lambos, etc.  1 of the biggest reasons why I love fieros so much is the appearance.  So why alter that if you "love" fieros?  Hmmm....<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_cut_sig_4.jpg">  <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierowrecker||09-09-2001||04:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B>Well, it's like this...there's so many of us here that like this car, yet we don't all want to be the same. So everyone likes to do something to be different, though we're all still alike. Did that make sense?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What he said...<P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||09-09-2001||05:28 PM||||I like modified fieros for several reasons.. <BR>1. improving performance, such as extra cooling, bigger brakes, engine swaps<BR>2. improved/updated looks<BR>3. fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
Z||000007||FieroFanaticus2||09-09-2001||09:42 PM||||Because it is one of the few cars that is actually AFFORDABLE to make mods on.  And because so many people decided to junk these cars instead of give them a loving home, they are one of the rarest affordable cars to work on.  I see maybe 3 or 4 Fieros any given week during the summer, and most of them are the same fiero's.  BUT, I see dozens of corvettes and mustangs and camaros, and firebirds, etc etc all over the place.  To a lot of us, it is exactly what the name FIERO means..... Pride ..... and I for one feel a lot of pride when I do something to make my fiero more unique.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dump_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Sootah||09-09-2001||11:34 PM||||Why? It's cheap (usually, anyway), there are lots of cool things you can do to it (engine swaps, Aus's side scoops, chop top) and its always cool to have a camaro pull up next to you and ya smoke him. Not that I have done that or even will, the car I am looking at is a 4-banger auto.<P>Speaking of mods, what can I do to the Duke (88) to make it just the teeniest bit faster? Short of tearing the engine apart. I am talking about cheap mods (K&N filter, etc)<P>Thanx<BR>-<B>Sootah</B><P>------------------<BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I><BR>AIM: KSSouter||||reg||1
Z||000009||Smoooooth GT||09-10-2001||12:49 AM||||Great Input everybody....  Mom said thank's for the replies..<BR>She said that she understand's and can see why we are as nutty as we are..lol<BR>she also said she understand's why we like to do mod's to our toy's to make them look different YET the same??..??  lol I guess all the females here will understand what she mean's..??  lol  Thanks again...  Steve<P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4.JPG"> ||||reg||1
